# Benchmark Rigor

- State the hypothesis, workload, input distribution, scale, metric, and
  acceptable regression before measuring.
- Separate setup, warmup, measurement, teardown, and correctness verification.
- Prevent dead-code elimination, cache accidents, hidden I/O, logging, and
  differing semantics from distorting comparisons.
- Record environment, versions, compiler flags, concurrency, repetitions, and
  dispersion, not only the best run.
- Compare like with like and report uncertainty, outliers, and practical
  significance.
- Retain a deterministic representative workload and a correctness oracle.
- Never claim an optimization from an unrepeatable single measurement.
